# D-229, symptom two: "a closed interval is history" is false of a shadow.
#
# A branch retires an edge it inherited by writing its own closed row at the
# ancestor's key — the only cross-lineage retirement Doctrine III permits.
# Archiving that row does not send history cold: it removes the branch's
# disbelief and lets the ancestor's open row win the resolution again, so the
# branch reaches a node it had stopped believing in. An operation that mints no
# assertions changed an answer.
#
# The guard is the `NOT EXISTS (… other.branch_id <> links.branch_id)` arm of
# the closed-interval clause. Remove it and this case fails.
fork parent=main child=x
retire key=0 branch=x
archive
